WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.962
After 1901, the Qing government carried out the New Policies reforms.

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:06.992
The government reformed the military, education, and administration.

00:00:06.992 --> 00:00:10.553
Officials busily discussed one new measure after another.

00:00:10.553 --> 00:00:13.935
New-style schools were established in places everywhere.

00:00:13.935 --> 00:00:16.620
Girls could also go to school to study now.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.810
The school gates were crowded with curious parents.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.645
Students studied mathematics, science, and foreign languages.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.720
In 1905, the imperial examination system was abolished.

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:32.732
The examination system that had lasted for a thousand years came to an end.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.417
The new-style army was neatly uniformed and trained strictly.

00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:39.801
He looked back once, with mixed feelings in his heart.

00:00:40.286 --> 00:00:44.587
Trains and the telegraph changed people's lives.

00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:47.961
Young people began to discuss new political ideas.

00:00:47.961 --> 00:00:51.240
The young soldiers were all full of energy and spirit.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.600
The reforms brought many new changes to society.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.339
But the dynasty's crisis still grew deeper and deeper.
